@doc \\`types` defines foundational types shared by the standard library.
\\
\\A consumer can repeatedly discard incoming values.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let discard: std::types::Consumer 'a (|) = fn _ => discard
\\```
module types
@doc \\`effects` defines reusable effects for control flow and passing values.
\\
\\A computation can request a configuration value through `Ask`.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let port = std::effects::!Ask ()
\\```
module effects
@doc \\`fs` provides file and directory operations through the `FileSystem` effect.
\\
\\A file can be replaced with UTF-8 text.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let save_notes = fn text =>
\\  std::fs::write_text "notes.txt" text
\\```
module fs
@doc \\`io` writes text to standard output and standard error through the `IO` effect.
\\
\\A greeting can be written as a line on standard output.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let greet = fn name =>
\\  std::io::println (std::str::concat "Hello, " name)
\\```
module io
@doc \\`process` reads process state and can exit the process.
\\
\\An environment variable lookup can return optional text or a process error.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let home = std::process::env "HOME"
\\```
module process
@doc \\`codec` defines format-independent encoders, decoders, and their protocols.
\\
\\A default codec can be derived for a record type.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\type Settings = { theme: String, retries: Nat }
\\
\\let settings_codec: Result (std::codec::Codec Settings) std::codec::DeriveError =
\\  std::codec::derive (std::reflect::mirror ())
\\```
module codec
@doc \\`json` parses, inspects, encodes, and decodes JSON documents.
\\
\\JSON text can be decoded directly into an expected Ruddy type.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let names: Result [String] std::json::Error =
\\  std::json::decode "[\"Ada\",\"Grace\"]"
\\```
module json
@doc \\`binary` encodes and decodes typed values in a positional binary format.
\\
\\A record can be encoded with its default positional binary codec.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let packet = std::binary::encode { sequence: 7n, message: "ready" }
\\```
module binary
@doc \\`url` parses and resolves URLs and provides immutable operations on their query parameters.
\\
\\An absolute URL can be parsed into a validated snapshot.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let endpoint = std::url::parse "https://api.example.com/users?page=2"
\\```
module url
@doc \\`http` sends buffered requests and provides helpers for common responses.
\\
\\A buffered `GET` request can use the default options.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let response = std::http::get "https://api.example.com/health"
\\```
module http
@if { platform: "node" }
@doc \\`path` supports host, POSIX, and Windows path conventions.
\\
\\Path segments can be joined using the host convention.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let config = std::path::join ["var", "lib", "ruddy", "config.json"]
\\```
module path
@doc \\`str` inspects, transforms, searches, and combines text by Unicode scalar value.
\\
\\Every plain occurrence of a substring can be replaced.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let redacted =
\\  std::str::replace_all ("Call 555-0100", "555-", "***-")
\\```
module str
@doc \\`nat` provides arithmetic, comparison, and conversion for natural numbers.
\\
\\A quantity can be kept within inclusive bounds.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let table_size = std::nat::clamp (requested_size, 1n, 12n)
\\```
module nat
@doc \\`int` provides arithmetic, comparison, conversion, and bounded operations for integers.
\\
\\A signed difference can be converted to a nonnegative distance.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let distance_from_zero = std::int::abs (-14i)
\\```
module int
@doc \\`real` provides arithmetic and mathematical functions for real numbers.
\\
\\An angle in degrees can be converted to radians.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let quarter_turn = std::real::degrees_to_radians 90.0
\\```
module real
@doc \\`boolean` provides logical operations and ordering for `Bool` values.
\\
\\An implication can require a true conclusion only when its premise is true.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let access_allowed =
\\  std::boolean::implies account_is_private viewer_follows_account
\\```
module boolean
@doc \\`option` defines optional values and functions for transforming and combining them.
\\
\\A fallback can replace an absent optional value.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let display_name = std::option::unwrap_or "Guest" saved_name
\\```
module option
@doc \\`result` defines and transforms successful or failed results.
\\
\\An error can be transformed without changing a successful value.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let readable_response =
\\  std::result::map_error (fn _ => "Request failed") response
\\```
module result
@doc \\`array` provides immutable operations on arrays.
\\
\\Available items can be kept in their original order.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let available_items = std::array::filter is_available inventory
\\```
module array
@doc \\`cell` creates and updates mutable cells whose effects stay within a tracked region.
\\
\\A mutable running total can be updated with a function.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let add_fee = fn subtotal => do
\\  let total = std::cell::new subtotal
\\  return std::cell::update (fn value => std::nat::add value 5n) total
\\end
\\```
module cell
@doc \\`any` packages a value with its type and recovers it through an exact type check.
\\
\\A packaged value can be recovered when the requested type matches exactly.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let stored = std::any::upcast "ready"
\\let status: Option String = std::any::downcast stored
\\```
module any
@doc \\`ffi` marks immediate foreign effects and converts values at foreign boundaries.
\\
\\A foreign value can be checked against an expected record shape.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let preferences: Result { dark_mode: Bool } std::ffi::DecodeError =
\\  std::ffi::decode foreign_preferences
\\```
module ffi
@doc \\`abi` validates C and WebAssembly component calling contracts.
\\
\\A scalar-only C calling plan can be validated for a 64-bit target.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let plan: std::abi::Plan = {
\\  name: "absolute_value",
\\  target: { convention: #C, address_bits: 64n, scalar_alignment: #None },
\\  parameters: [{
\\    name: "value",
\\    shape: #Scalar (#Integer { bits: 32n, signed: true }),
\\  }],
\\  result: #Some (#Scalar (#Integer { bits: 32n, signed: true })),
\\  obligations: [],
\\}
\\
\\let validation = std::abi::validate plan
\\```
module abi
@doc \\`js` converts and observes values at JavaScript boundaries.
\\
\\A Ruddy record can be lowered into host data for JavaScript.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let host_user = std::js::lower { name: "Ada", active: true }
\\```
module js
@doc \\`reflect` describes types as data through compiler-supplied mirrors.
\\
\\A value's static type can be described as ordinary data.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let schema = std::reflect::describe (
\\  std::reflect::type_of { name: "Ada", active: true }
\\)
\\```
module reflect
@doc \\`function` provides combinators for applying, composing, and adapting functions.
\\
\\Two transformations can be composed into one function.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let double_after_increment = std::function::compose
\\  (fn value => std::nat::multiply value 2n)
\\  (fn value => std::nat::add value 1n)
\\```
module function
@doc \\`tuple` constructs, reads, swaps, and transforms tuple values.
\\
\\The second value of a pair can be transformed without changing the first.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let updated_price = std::tuple::map_second
\\  (fn cents => std::nat::add cents 200n)
\\  ("coffee", 300n)
\\```
module tuple
@doc \\`order` defines three-way ordering and builds comparisons from ordering functions.
\\
\\Records can be compared by projecting a field before applying an ordering.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\let compare_by_age =
\\  std::order::compare_by std::nat::compare (fn person => person.age)
\\```
module order
@doc \\`prelude` contains the types, effects, and values available without an explicit import.
\\
\\A line can be written without a module qualifier.
\\
\\```ruddy
\\println "ready"
\\```
module prelude

@private
type Option 't = #Some 't | #None
@private
type Result 'some 'error = #Some 'some | #Error 'error
